  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `fold_warnings_located` (`crates/ui/src/operations.rs`) groups `Warning::DrillUndersize` under key `223`. Before, it used `216`. That is the key of `Warning::AvoidHit` with `FixturePart::Shank` (the avoid range is `216..=220`).\n- A group prints only the line of its first warning. When the undersize hole came first, the pane folded the blocking \"Do not touch\" shank hit into the advisory line as \"repeated on 1 more move\". The pane did not show the shank hit.\n- `UndercutLift` (added on main by #1444, commit 5452810e5) groups under key `222`. Main gave it `217`, the key of `Warning::AvoidHit` with `FixturePart::Holder`: the same fault. The merge of main (9f1f7adb1) moves it.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3040-drill-undersize-fold-key.md`.\n\n## Pinning test\n\n`operations::warning_fold_tests::a_drill_undersize_never_hides_an_avoid_hit` folds one `DrillUndersize` and one `AvoidHit` for each of the five `FixturePart` values. It asserts six lines, each with its own move.\n\nWith the old key the test fails, and the output shows the defect:\n\n```\n\"warning: undersize hole at move 3: ... - repeated on 1 more move (to 10)\",\n\"warning: holder at move 11 violates protected 'Do not touch' item #1 (0.500 mm short of clearance)\",\n...\n```\n\nThe shank hit at move 10 has no line of its own.\n\n`operations::warning_fold_tests::an_undercut_lift_never_hides_an_avoid_hit` folds one `UndercutLift`, one `DrillUndersize` and one `AvoidHit` for each `FixturePart`. It asserts seven lines. With main's key `217` for `UndercutLift`, it fails.\n\n## Gates\n\nHead 9f1f7adb1 (main 2d98d87be merged in):\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 3 steps, 0 failed (`ui build`, `ui suites: lib`, `ui suites: operations`).\n- `warning_fold_tests`: 8 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run`: the diff reaches no heavy lane.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe operation page with four warnings on one path: an undersize hole (move 3), a \"Do not touch\" hit of the shank (move 10), an undercut lift (move 12), and a \"Do not touch\" hit of the holder (move 14). The status banner is open. The images are on the images-only `pr-screenshots` branch of the fork, not on this branch.\n\n- Before (main, keys 216 and 217): \"2 warnings\". The undersize line holds the shank hit as \"repeated on 1 more move (to 10)\". The undercut line holds the holder hit as \"(to 14)\". The two \"Do not touch\" hits have no line.\n- After (this PR, keys 223 and 222): \"4 warnings\". Each \"Do not touch\" hit has its own line.\n\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| ![before: 2 warnings](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3062/before-strip.png) | ![after: 4 warnings](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3062/after-strip.png) |\n\nFull frames: [before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3062/before-full.png), [after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3062/after-full.png).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No check in the running app window. The screenshots come from an off-screen render of the real operation page, with the four warnings put into a generated Face path by a temporary test (not committed). The pane text does not change for a program with only one of the two warnings.\n- `crates/ui/src/operations.rs` was 635 lines before this PR, above the 400-line rule. It is 685 lines after the merge. This PR adds 40 lines (the two new tests are in the `warning_fold_tests` module, as the issue asks). It does not split the file.\n\nChangelog: The Warnings pane shows a protected \"Do not touch\" shank hit on its own line when the same program also has an undersize-hole warning or an undercut-lift warning.\n\nBranch made from `upstream/main` at 08697d3c4.\n\nFixes #3040\nFixes #3260\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
